releases.body:
@es3d/es3d/stage lets a page move its own shapes. setTransform(id, matrix) writes a column-major matrix onto an element that appears once. A shared definition, or a <repeat> or <scatter> copy, is left as the file drew it.

The converter, Studio and the es3d command now read and write X3D, USDA and OpenSCAD, and write a three.js module. X3D export is Classic (.x3dv). USD is USDA text. OpenSCAD is read. The three.js file is export only. --flatten writes the same triangles as glTF.

Some of these convertors are a bit shaky, so I expect there may be need to update them later down the line.
